DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The pptthhrreeaadd__bbaarrrriieerr__iinniitt() function will initialize _b_a_r_r_i_e_r with at‐
     tributes specified in _a_t_t_r, or if it is NULL, with default attributes.
     The number of threads that must call pptthhrreeaadd__bbaarrrriieerr__wwaaiitt() before any of
     the waiting threads can be released is specified by _c_o_u_n_t.  The
     pptthhrreeaadd__bbaarrrriieerr__ddeessttrrooyy() function will destroy _b_a_r_r_i_e_r and release any
     resources that may have been allocated on its behalf.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__bbaarrrriieerr__wwaaiitt() function will synchronize calling threads at
     _b_a_r_r_i_e_r.  The threads will be blocked from making further progress until
     a sufficient number of threads calls this function.  The number of
     threads that must call it before any of them will be released is deter‐
     mined by the _c_o_u_n_t argument to pptthhrreeaadd__bbaarrrriieerr__iinniitt().  Once the threads
     have been released the barrier will be reset.

